Taxi Cab Revenue Dataset: Payment Type Analysis

This dataset contains information on taxi trips, including payment methods, fare amounts, and other trip-related details. It is designed to help analyze the relationship between payment types (credit card vs. cash) and total fare amounts, providing insights into strategies for maximizing taxi driver revenue.

Key Columns in the Dataset:
Trip ID:

Description: Unique identifier for each trip.
Data Type: Integer
Total Fare Amount:

Description: The total fare charged for the taxi ride, including any applicable charges such as tips or surcharges.
Data Type: Float
Payment Type:

Description: The method of payment used by the customer for the trip. This can either be "Credit Card" or "Cash."
Data Type: Categorical (String)
Trip Duration:

Description: The duration of the taxi ride in minutes.
Data Type: Float
Trip Distance:

Description: The total distance covered during the taxi ride, typically in kilometers or miles.
Data Type: Float
Pickup Date/Time:

Description: The date and time when the taxi ride started.
Data Type: DateTime
Dropoff Date/Time:

Description: The date and time when the taxi ride ended.
Data Type: DateTime
Driver ID:

Description: Unique identifier for the driver of the taxi.
Data Type: Integer
City/Region:

Description: The location where the taxi ride took place (city or region).
Data Type: String
Purpose of the Dataset:
This dataset will be analyzed to explore whether payment types (credit card vs. cash) have an impact on total fare amounts. By identifying any trends, the goal is to provide actionable insights that can help taxi drivers optimize revenue, either by encouraging the use of certain payment methods or adjusting pricing strategies.
